# rcas is a computer algebra system written in plain Ruby.
# Ruby symbols are the indeterminates - no new language, no new parser.
(x + 1) * (1 - x)

# Nothing is rewritten until you ask for it.
((x + 1) * (1 - x)).expand

# Arithmetic stays exact - never a float by accident.
1/3r + 1/6r
sqrt(8)

# Calculus, the way you would write it on paper:
diff(sin(x**2), x)
integrate(1/(x**2 + 1), x)

# And when rcas cannot do it, it says so. It never guesses.
integrate(sin(x)/log(x), x)

# Equations are solved exactly, radicals and all:
solve(x**2 - 2, x)
factor(x**4 - 1)

# The chat front end can typeset its answers.
/output typeset
sum(k**2, k, 1, n)
integrate(x*exp(x), x)

# Every line above is valid Ruby - this script is itself
# a session you can paste straight into rcas.
